  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme for Country Partnership (PCP) Ethiopia Phase II (2025 # 2030)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ethiopia has been implementing PCP since March 2015 as one of the two pilot countries selected for testing the partnership model. The PCP Ethiopia (PCP ETH) pilot phase has exceeded expectations, demonstrating remarkable progress in partnership building, resource mobilization, investment promotion. These efforts have accelerated the development of industrial infrastructure, including the Integrated Agro-Industrial Parks (IAIPs) and Modjo Leather City (MLC).  The partnership platform created through PCP has successfully mitigated inefficiencies in programme management by reducing fragmentations, redundancies and lack of focus. In addition, it has fostered greater alignment, collective action, unity of purpose and ensuring that resources both financial and human are concentrated on high-impact areas for optimal results. In a context like Ethiopia, where institutional capacity constraints are widespread, attempting to address all challenges simultaneously can be counterproductive.  Encouraged by the substantial progress achieved over the past ten years, the Ethiopian government is taking measures to institutionalize and mainstream the PCP approach. This includes, expanding its mandate to address implementation challenges and improve output delivery. Furthermore, the PCP ETH leadership team seeks to enhance its coo</narrative>
  </description>
